#: ../../source/methods/augmentation.rst:3
msgid ""
"Simulate real-world variations in your spectral data to enhance model "
"robustness. This can include introducing controlled noise, baseline "
"shifts, or small wavelength misalignments to mimic real measurement "
"conditions. By doing so, your model learns to handle variability in "
"experimental setups, instrument performance, and sample "
"preparation—leading to more reliable predictions when applied to unseen "
"data."
